From c7b6d2a8915ecea4562000d81aafa3c7f56e3e21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Keep server fallback when browser-only content suspends
 on the client

When `use(browser())` bails out on the server, Fizz emits the boundary as a
client-rendered fallback (`<!--$!-->`). On the client we retry the content
without hydrating. If that render suspends again, e.g. on a promise created
on the client (setTimeout, localStorage, IndexedDB), we used to delete the
dehydrated server fallback and mount an identical client fallback in its
place. That recreates the fallback DOM and restarts CSS animations.

Instead, if the client render suspends and the boundary's props didn't
change, stay in the dehydrated state and leave the server fallback in place
until the content can render. The work loop already supports this state for
pending boundaries: the rest of the tree commits and the boundary is retried
when the promise resolves. This is limited to browser-only bailouts. Server
errors keep the current behavior, because each retry would report the
server error again.

Fixes #37620
